    description: "OWNER RULING 2026-10-25: delete validate_pass_dependencies, and add the two static depends_on checks it never made.\n\nWHY. catalog.py:262 validate_pass_dependencies(active_passes) is a pre-run CNF membership gate that raises. ADR-0056 W1 refused to wire it (\"raising is the withholding direction\"; WI-jijor found 261 of 893 surveys, 29.2%, with a falsified declaration) and kept it only \"as-is so its 11 tests stay green\". Its jobs are done by three wired mechanisms: validate_pass_name_resolution (CI, TestCatalogStaticConsistency, can fail: a >=50-clause floor and a pinned declaration), prerequisite_absent_clauses (runtime disclosure at linkers/registry.py:828-857), find_falsified_dependencies (post-run declaration audit, cli.py:13540-13554). Measured 2026-10-25: on a 1 .js + 1 .rs Tauri fixture it raises on 12 of 71 active passes, every one a repo-lacks-the-language case; over the full catalog it cannot fail once name resolution holds. Only callers: 11 tests in test_catalog.py; listed on .ci/test-only-reachability-baseline.json. ADR-0030 :88/:95/:118 claim it runs at configuration time; it never has.\n\nDO (one PR).\n1. Delete the function, its module-docstring paragraph, the Pass.depends_on docstring paragraph, the 'Distinct from validate_pass_dependencies' paragraph in validate_pass_name_resolution, and the cross-references in find_falsified_dependencies / emit_falsified_dependency_summary; pass_silence.py:694; TestValidatePassDependencies and its import; the baseline key (shrink-only, removal allowed). validate_pass_name_resolution stays and its docstring says why: its reader is a CI test that can fail.\n2. ADR-0030 and ADR-0056 edited in place to the final design (no history): depends_on declares prerequisites, the runtime never gates on them, three wired mechanisms check or disclose them. ADR-0056 W1 names find_falsified_dependencies; re-decide item 1 (a pass-level selector) stays as the trigger, answered by a DISCLOSURE that separates 'removed by the selector' from 'no files', not by a raise.\n3. Static check G5: validate_pass_name_resolution rejects an empty INNER clause ([[]], an unsatisfiable OR of nothing); an outer [] (the provably-consumes-nothing declaration) stays legal. Live declarations carry none. Control: a [[]] fixture fails.\n4. Static check G4: for every linker literal in a linker's depends_on, the depended-on linker's priority is STRICTLY lower (same-priority linkers run in parallel from one snapshot, registry.py:1011-1015). Today: graphql-sdl 55 -> graphql 60, graphql-resolver 60; inheritance 15 -> type-hierarchy 60. Controls: a floor (>=3 linker literals) and a mutation (graphql-sdl at 60 turns it red).\n5. CHANGELOG (Removed + Added). No output, schema or governance change.\nRelated: INV-hujog (restated 2026-10-25), the G1 item filed beside this one."  # a63e
    fields: {}  # a63e
