  message: "DONE in PR #1864 (merged to dev as f0b360e93c, rebased from 0ed6a63ec5). Verified in-process on merged dev, not inferred from the diff: hasattr(hypergumbo_core.catalog, 'validate_pass_dependencies') is False, and a whole-tree grep of packages/, docs/adr/ and .ci/ finds 0 references. validate_pass_name_resolution([Pass('odd-linker', depends_on=[[]])]) raises \"Pass 'odd-linker' depends_on empty clause []\". The live catalog resolves with no empty clause. Live linker-order violations: []. With graphql-sdl-linker moved to priority 60 the same predicate reports [(graphql-linker, graphql-sdl-linker), (graphql-resolver-linker, graphql-sdl-linker)], so the ordering check can fail. Pre-merge: full affected smart-test (786 files) 24540 passed, 4 skipped, 7 xfailed; all changed sources at 100% coverage; mypy ratchet clean; PR CI green. ADR-0030 and ADR-0056 W1 corrected in place; test-only baseline shrank by one key. No output, schema or governance change. INV-hujog stays violated on WI-nijil and the WI-rasal family. NOTE: the short id 'WI-rihob' is shared with WI-rihob-rupar (stable_id on container kinds); the catalog.py docstring and the INV-hujog note cite it short -- this item is WI-rihob-fufiz."  # ddde
